# The recorded oracle fixtures are machine-generated: they are what the
# predecessor implementation actually returned, captured call by call. Nobody
# reads or reviews them by hand, and left as ordinary source they would
# dominate the language statistics and bury the real change in any commit that
# re-records them.
#
# `linguist-generated` and not `-diff`: GitHub collapses the file in review but
# the diff stays available. A re-recorded fixture means the predecessor's
# behaviour changed, which is exactly the thing a reviewer must be able to look
# at — suppressing the diff would hide the only evidence of it.
tests/fixtures/oracle/** linguist-generated

# Line endings. Some of the material this package grew out of came from
# Windows, and a mixed checkout makes every subsequent diff unreadable.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
